61411.sol:
$\begin{aligned}& x²+y²+\mathrm{a} x+\mathrm{b} y=0 \\
& \Rightarrow\left( x+\frac{\mathrm{a}}{2}\right)^2+\left( y+\frac{\mathrm{b}}{2}\right)^2=\frac{\mathrm{a}^2+\mathrm{b}^2}{4}
\end{aligned}$ Comparing with $(x-\mathrm{h})^2+(y-\mathrm{k})^2=\mathrm{r}^2$, we get $\mathrm{h}=-\frac{\mathrm{a}}{2}, \mathrm{k}=-\frac{\mathrm{b}}{2}, \mathrm{r}=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{a}^2+\mathrm{b}^2}{4}}\therefore \quad$ The parametric equations are x=-$\frac{\mathrm{a}}{2}+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{a}^2+\mathrm{b}^2}{4}} \cos \theta,$ y=-$\frac{\mathrm{b}}{2}+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{a}^2+\mathrm{b}^2}{4}} \sin \theta$

